    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **260 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made the endpoint return it.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 replaced the three separate 409 checks (telephone-in-use, email-in-use, household-member-without-`sharesHousehold`) with one check against a derived key:\n   ```\n   identityKey = normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + (householdId or \"\")\n   ```\n   A create is now rejected with 409 only when the new owner's **whole** identity key equals an existing owner's. The new owner's prospective `householdId` is computed before the check (so it participates in the key), and the existing household-id assignment logic was preserved and refactored to reuse it. Added a private `identityKey(...)` helper.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `formatIdentityKey(owner)` and mapped it to the new `identityKey` DTO field, so the key is derived from the stored (already E.164-normalized telephone, lower-cased email, stored household id) fields and returned on every owner response.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec).\n\n**Behavioural effect (as the spec requires):** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have distinct identity keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. This intentionally relaxes the old \"reject a second same-household member unless `sharesHousehold`\" rule.\n\nOne thing worth noting: the existing `householdId` seed in the controller uses a literal NUL byte (`\"\\0\"`) as its separator rather than a space (visible only in a hex dump) \u2014 I left that untouched since it's pre-existing and unrelated, but flagging it in case it's a surprise.",
